      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Freedom of Speech and Expression</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">News and News Media</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Suits and Litigation (Civil)</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_org">CNN</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_org">MS NOW</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_org">Politico, The</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Trump, Donald J</category>
      <media:content height="1800" medium="image" url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/09/23/multimedia/23biz-media-ban-ruling-hfo-hclw/23biz-media-ban-ruling-hfo-hclw-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" width="1800"></media:content>
      <media:credit>Haiyun Jiang/The New York Times</media:credit>
      <media:description>CNN, MS Now and Politico had sued the administration after they were banned from the White House.</media:description>
    </item>
<item>
      <title>Iowa Judge Dismisses Trump’s Lawsuit Against The Des Moines Register</title>
      <link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/23/us/politics/des-moines-register-trump-lawsuit.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/23/us/politics/des-moines-register-trump-lawsuit.html</guid>
      <atom:link href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/23/us/politics/des-moines-register-trump-lawsuit.html" rel="standout"></atom:link>
      <description>The suit challenged a poll that showed Trump trailing Kamala Harris in the final weeks of the 2024 race. A judge warned that similar legal challenges could have a chilling effect on news reporting.</description>
      <dc:creator>Ishani Desai</dc:creator>
      <pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 02:07:27 +0000</pubDate>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">United States Politics and Government</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Suits and Litigation (Civil)</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Polls and Public Opinion</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Selzer, Ann (1956- )</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Trump, Donald J</category>
      <media:content height="1799" medium="image" url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/09/23/multimedia/23xp-selzer-mqkb/23xp-selzer-mqkb-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" width="1800"></media:content>
      <media:credit>Chip Somodevilla/Getty Images</media:credit>
      <media:description>A poll published by The Des Moines Register in 2024 showed Donald J. Trump trailing Kamala Harris in Iowa. Mr. Trump went on to win the state by double digits.</media:description>
    </item>
<item>
      <title>As Xi Visits Washington, Trump Plays Down China’s Actions Against U.S. Interests</title>
      <link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/23/us/politics/trump-xi-china-visit.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/23/us/politics/trump-xi-china-visit.html</guid>
      <atom:link href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/23/us/politics/trump-xi-china-visit.html" rel="standout"></atom:link>
      <description>Despite the rivalry between the United States and China, President Trump has repeatedly found ways to give President Xi Jinping of China a pass, portraying him more as a personal friend than a competitor.</description>
      <dc:creator>Erica L. Green</dc:creator>
      <pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:14:18 +0000</pubDate>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">United States Politics and Government</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">International Relations</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Trump, Donald J</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_geo">United States</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_geo">China</category>
      <media:content height="1800" medium="image" url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/09/23/multimedia/23dc-prexy-01-qbwc/23dc-prexy-01-qbwc-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" width="1800"></media:content>
      <media:credit>Kenny Holston/The New York Times</media:credit>
      <media:description>President Trump has spent weeks dismissing or excusing reports of China’s infractions as he’s prepared for the “great honor” of hosting President Xi Jinping in Washington.</media:description>
    </item>
